`EntryFanOut` is a small **utility class I introduced two answers ago** (in the "call the REST API for each `RedisEntry`" response). It's not a Spring or Reactor class — it's your own helper that encapsulates the "**run one async action per Redis entry, with bounded concurrency and a chosen failure policy**" logic, so the base class and every handler don't have to re-implement it.

Here it is again, complete and self-contained, plus exactly how `NationalCodeLookupHandler` uses it.

---

## 1. What problem it solves

Inside `NationalCodeLookupHandler.onMatch(...)` you have a `List<RedisEntry>` and need to call `onMatchedEntry(...)` for each. Doing that naively:

```java
Flux.fromIterable(entries).flatMap(e -> onMatchedEntry(payload, nc, e, ctx)).then();
```

has three problems: unbounded parallelism, fail-fast semantics (first error cancels the rest, even though some calls already succeeded), and no visibility into *which* entries failed. `EntryFanOut` fixes all three in one place.

---

## 2. The code

```java
package com.example.ncc.core.fanout;

import lombok.extern.slf4j.Slf4j;
import reactor.core.publisher.Flux;
import reactor.core.publisher.Mono;

import java.util.List;
import java.util.function.Function;

/** Runs one reactive action per RedisEntry with bounded concurrency and a failure policy. */
@Slf4j
public final class EntryFanOut {

    private EntryFanOut() {}

    public enum FailurePolicy {
        /** First error cancels remaining calls and fails the message. */
        FAIL_FAST,
        /** Attempt every entry; if any failed, fail the message with details of the failed ones. */
        TRY_ALL_THEN_FAIL,
        /** Attempt every entry; log failures; never fail the message. */
        BEST_EFFORT
    }

    public static Mono<Void> run(List<RedisEntry> entries,
                                 Function<RedisEntry, Mono<Void>> action,
                                 int concurrency,
                                 FailurePolicy policy) {

        if (entries == null || entries.isEmpty()) {
            return Mono.empty();
        }

        return switch (policy) {

            case FAIL_FAST -> Flux.fromIterable(entries)
                    .flatMap(action, concurrency)
                    .then();

            case BEST_EFFORT -> Flux.fromIterable(entries)
                    .flatMap(e -> action.apply(e)
                            .doOnError(t -> log.warn("Entry action failed (best-effort) key={}", e.key(), t))
                            .onErrorResume(t -> Mono.empty()), concurrency)
                    .then();

            case TRY_ALL_THEN_FAIL -> Flux.fromIterable(entries)
                    .flatMap(e -> action.apply(e)
                            .thenReturn(EntryResult.ok(e))
                            .onErrorResume(t -> Mono.just(EntryResult.failed(e, t))), concurrency)
                    .collectList()
                    .flatMap(results -> {
                        List<EntryResult> failed = results.stream().filter(EntryResult::isFailure).toList();
                        return failed.isEmpty()
                                ? Mono.<Void>empty()
                                : Mono.error(new PartialFailureException(entries.size(), failed));
                    });
        };
    }
}
```

Supporting types:

```java
/** Outcome of the action for one entry. */
public record EntryResult(RedisEntry entry, Throwable error) {
    public static EntryResult ok(RedisEntry e)                  { return new EntryResult(e, null); }
    public static EntryResult failed(RedisEntry e, Throwable t) { return new EntryResult(e, t); }
    public boolean isFailure() { return error != null; }
}
```

```java
/** Thrown by TRY_ALL_THEN_FAIL when at least one entry action failed. */
@Getter
public class PartialFailureException extends RuntimeException {

    private final int total;
    private final List<EntryResult> failed;

    public PartialFailureException(int total, List<EntryResult> failed) {
        super(failed.size() + "/" + total + " entry actions failed: "
                + failed.stream().map(f -> f.entry().key()).collect(Collectors.joining(",")));
        this.total = total;
        this.failed = failed;
    }

    /** Handy for the DLT header so a replay tool can re-run only these keys. */
    public List<String> failedKeys() {
        return failed.stream().map(f -> f.entry().key()).toList();
    }
}
```

