## 3. How `NationalCodeLookupHandler` uses it

```java
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public abstract class NationalCodeLookupHandler<T> implements TopicHandler<T> {

    protected final NationalCodeLookup lookup;

    // ---- what each concrete handler fills in ----
    protected abstract String extractNationalCode(T payload);
    protected abstract Mono<Void> onMatchedEntry(T payload, String nationalCode, RedisEntry entry, MessageContext ctx);

    // ---- knobs with sensible defaults ----
    protected boolean accepts(RedisEntry entry)                    { return true; }
    protected int entryConcurrency()                               { return 8; }
    protected EntryFanOut.FailurePolicy failurePolicy()            { return EntryFanOut.FailurePolicy.TRY_ALL_THEN_FAIL; }
    protected Mono<Void> onNoMatch(T payload, String nc, MessageContext ctx) { return Mono.empty(); }

    /** Default: fan out one onMatchedEntry call per entry. Override for a single batched call. */
    protected Mono<Void> onMatch(T payload, String nc, List<RedisEntry> entries, MessageContext ctx) {
        List<RedisEntry> relevant = entries.stream().filter(this::accepts).toList();

        return EntryFanOut.run(
                relevant,
                entry -> onMatchedEntry(payload, nc, entry, ctx),   // the action
                entryConcurrency(),                                 // max parallel calls per message
                failurePolicy());                                   // what to do on partial failure
    }

    @Override
    public final Mono<Void> handle(T payload, MessageContext ctx) {
        String nc = extractNationalCode(payload);
        if (nc == null || nc.isBlank()) {
            return Mono.error(new InvalidMessageException("nationalCode missing"));
        }
        return lookup.findAll(nc)
                .collectList()
                .flatMap(entries -> entries.isEmpty()
                        ? onNoMatch(payload, nc, ctx)
                        : onMatch(payload, nc, entries, ctx));
    }
}
```

Flow for one message:

```
handle()
 └─ lookup.findAll(nc)  ──► [entry1, entry2, entry3]
     └─ onMatch()
         └─ EntryFanOut.run(entries, e -> onMatchedEntry(...), 8, TRY_ALL_THEN_FAIL)
              ├─ onMatchedEntry(entry1) ─► API ✔
              ├─ onMatchedEntry(entry2) ─► API ✘
              └─ onMatchedEntry(entry3) ─► API ✔
              → all three attempted, then Mono.error(PartialFailureException("1/3 failed: entry2Key"))
                → pipeline sends the record to DLT with x-failed-keys header
```

