## 4. Using the failure detail in the DLT publisher

Since `PartialFailureException` knows which keys failed, expose that in the dead-letter record:

```java
public Mono<Void> publish(ReceiverRecord<String, byte[]> rec, Throwable err) {
    var out = new ProducerRecord<>(rec.topic() + ".DLT", rec.key(), rec.value());
    out.headers().add("x-error", err.toString().getBytes(UTF_8));
    out.headers().add("x-origin-offset", String.valueOf(rec.offset()).getBytes(UTF_8));
    if (err instanceof PartialFailureException pfe) {
        out.headers().add("x-failed-keys", String.join(",", pfe.failedKeys()).getBytes(UTF_8));
    }
    return sender.send(Mono.just(SenderRecord.create(out, null))).then()
                 .onErrorResume(e -> Mono.empty());
}
```

